#!/usr/bin/env sh

# THE CHECKS, AT COMMIT TIME.
#
# Owner: "remove ci for captain. make it inside commit."
#
# The APK workflow is gone, so this is not a second opinion any more - it is
# the only one. That is why it runs the whole thing rather than a quick subset:
# a gate that checks less than the gate it replaced is not a gate.
#
#   unit suite      about 6 seconds
#   browser suite   about 6 minutes
#
# Six minutes is a real cost and it is deliberate, because the alternative is
# nothing at all. Two things follow from it:
#
#   Commit in batches rather than every few lines. The suite does not care how
#   many changes it is checking.
#
#   `git commit --no-verify` when you genuinely need to save your place - a
#   half-written thought, a stash by another name. Nothing downstream will
#   catch it, so use it knowing that.
#
# TURN IT ON, ONCE PER CLONE:
#
#     git config core.hooksPath .githooks
#
# Not installed for you. A hook that appears unasked and takes six minutes the
# first time somebody fixes a typo is a hook that gets switched off, and then
# there is no gate anywhere.
#
# release.yml stays on GitHub: it needs a JDK, an Android SDK, a keystore and a
# macOS runner, and none of that belongs on a laptop.

# Tests create temporary repositories. Do not let the parent commit's Git
# environment point those fixtures back at this worktree.
unset $(git rev-parse --local-env-vars)
npm run check
